  "key_findings": [
    "Overall MI = 0.0373 bits (NMI = 0.0331): trust and significance share modest but non-zero information across all domains.",
    "H(Trust) = 2.1431 bits (82.9% of theoretical maximum), indicating substantial grade diversity.",
    "Neurological domain has highest NMI = 0.3117 (n=27), suggesting trust is most predictive of significance there.",
    "Renal domain shows MI ~ 0, indicating grade is uninformative about significance in that domain (n=13)."
  ],
  "method": "Shannon entropy H(X)=-sum(p_i*log2(p_i)); KL divergence D_KL(P||Q)=sum(P_i*log2(P_i/Q_i)); MI computed from 6x2 contingency table (grade x significant); NMI=MI/sqrt(H(Trust)*H(Sig)); all per domain."
